= Distributed cognition — Simple =

'''Distributed cognition''' is the idea that some thinking tasks are best understood as happening across a system of people, tools, and information, not only inside one person's head.

A ship's navigation team might use several people, charts, instruments, and spoken updates. Together, the system performs a task that no one person is doing alone.

A notebook, checklist, map, or computer can also become part of how a person solves a problem.

This does not mean a group has a magical group mind.

It means the useful boundary for studying a cognitive task can sometimes include the environment and tools.

